<title>USA: US Airways in talks to buy regional jets.</title>
<headline>US Airways in talks to buy regional jets.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>US Airways Group Inc is in talks with aircraft manufacturers to buy an unspecified number of regional jets, Stephen Wolf, the company's chairman, said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The regional aircraft would be operated by US Airways' commuter subsidiaries, not by the main airline, Wolf said.</p>
<p>&quot;We started talks with regional jet makers, of which there are four. We believe there are two which are appropriate,&quot; Wolf told reporters after the company's annual meeting in Philadelphia.</p>
